<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by an unhandled `std::invalid_argument` exception in the `Pistache::Http::(anonymous namespace)::parse_epoch` function, located in `/src/pistache/src/common/http_defs.cc`.

Analysis:
The fuzz driver generates an empty string for `date_string` and passes it to `Pistache::Http::FullDate::fromString`. This function, in turn, calls `parse_epoch` with the empty string. Inside `parse_epoch`, the code attempts to convert the string to a number using `std::stoull(s)` at line 75. According to the C++ standard, `std::stoull` throws `std::invalid_argument` if the input string does not contain any digits and cannot be converted. The existing `try-catch` block only handles `std::out_of_range` exceptions, not `std::invalid_argument`. Consequently, the exception is unhandled, leading to program termination.

Suggestion for patching the project:
Add a check at the beginning of the `parse_epoch` function in `/src/pistache/src/common/http_defs.cc` to handle empty strings.

```cpp
// Before line 67
if (s.empty())
return false;
```
Alternatively, modify the `catch` block to also handle `std::invalid_argument`:
```cpp
// Change line 77
catch (const std::logic_error& e) // Catches both invalid_argument and out_of_range
{
return false;
}
```
</crash-analysis>

